var _gate: Callable = _default_gate  # can't default to method reference at init time? Use _gate_valid flag or _gate := Callable() with _has_gate? Simpler: var _gate: Callable; var _gate_set := false. Or make _always_true a static func, _gate assigned in _init? RefCounted's _init runs on new() — fine, no args needed. But FSM style avoids _init. Let's use _gate_set flag… actually simpler: _default_gate is a static func, so `var _gate: Callable = _default_gate` as member default? Can't reference static function as default for member var? In GDScript 4, you can assign a Callable to a var. `var _gate: Callable = _always_true_callable` — the default value expression is evaluated at instance construction; referencing a static function of the same class as a bare identifier… `Callable(self, "_always_true")` on an instance calls the instance's method. Is a bare function name in GDScript 4 a Callable? Yes: in GDScript 2.0 bare identifier of a method = Callable(self, name). Static functions have `Class.func`. Member default `= _always_true` — allowed? Function-to-Callable conversion in defaults… in GDScript 2.0 bare function name is a callable in expressions (first-class). To avoid doubt, safer to use a lazy check: `if not _gate_set: return true`.
var _log_seq := 0
var _transaction_log: Array = []
