if state == null: NULL_GAME_STATE
state_code := _validate_state(state); if code fail(code)  # BAD_STATE/BAD_PRICE
if not (sale_event_id is String) or empty: BAD_EVENT_ID
if not (instance_ids is Variant array?) → check `instance_ids is Array`; empty → BAD_INSTANCE_LIST; element is non-empty String else BAD_INSTANCE_LIST
Dedupe preserving order → dedup_ids
Fingerprint fp_ids := dedup_ids sorted (order-independent)
if _sale_ledger.has(sid):
    if _sale_ledger[sid] == fp_ids (array of string compare — String has == so array == is fine): ALREADY_APPLIED ok:true gold_added 0
    else CONFLICT_SALE_PARAMS
# Existence check and pricing
var price_sum := 0
For each id in dedup: if not in basket → UNKNOWN_INSTANCE
Prices from basket fish's sale_price_at_catch (validated non-negative int by state validation… BAD_PRICE is covered there — plan lists BAD_PRICE in E4 "负价格/畸形篮元素" via corrupted basket). But state validation already scans basket elements — corrupt fish price → BAD_STATE? Earlier we decided price-invalid element → BAD_PRICE in _validate_state. So commit_catch into a state with corrupt price fish also → BAD_PRICE. That's consistent with plan's "篮内价格非非负整数 → BAD_PRICE".
# Overflow
var new_gold := state.wallet_gold + price_sum  — check overflow first: if price_sum > INT64_MAX - wallet → GOLD_OVERFLOW
Build next state: basket without sold IDs, wallet=new_gold, processed_sale_ids+sid, revision+1
Ledger: new sale ledger
gate → PERSIST_FAILED zero side effect
Publish: state.basket = filter (assign new array); wallet_gold; processed_sale_ids.append; revision+=1; _sale_ledger[sid]=fp_ids
Return {ok:true, code:"", gold_added: price_sum}
