Set equivalence: ledger.processed_catches.keys() as set == set(state.processed_catch_ids); same for sale.
Also: instance IDs in sale fingerprints should not exist in basket (a sold fish is no longer in basket) → BAD_LEDGER on mismatch. Hmm, what's restore_ledger's stable error code? Plan's code list doesn't have a code for restore… "restore_ledger … fail-closed". Use BAD_STATE? Better a dedicated code "BAD_LEDGER". Plan's stable code list says those are for commands (commit/sell errors). restore/snapshot/set_gate are auxiliary. Introduce "BAD_LEDGER" for restore failure — document. Or keep within plan's list… list is "稳定错误码" for commands; adding one for ledger restore is an extension not a change. Let's use BAD_LEDGER and document in report.
Success: replace _catch_ledger/_sale_ledger with deep copies; log. Return {ok:true, code:""}.
