Also should commit_catch reject if catch ID is in state.processed_catch_ids but not in _catch_ledger (fresh service without restore)? E11 covers this by restore_ledger. But if service has ledger containing ID in state.processed_catch_ids? Inconsistent authority… Plan says the ledger must be consistent with state.processed_*_ids at restore time. For commit: state has ID in processed_catch_ids but ledger doesn't — fish was committed by previous service; a fresh service without restore might duplicate the fish! Fail-closed: if state.processed_catch_ids has the ID but ledger doesn't → CONFLICT? Hmm. Simplest fail-closed: if ID ∈ state.processed_catch_ids but ID ∉ ledger → "LEDGER_STATE_MISMATCH" reject… This is a nice safety, but adds a code not in plan. Or require consistency: check at command level: if processed list has ID → treat as already-applied but can't verify fingerprint → CONFLICT_CATCH_PARAMS (can't verify). I think a clean approach: _catch_ledger.has(cid) OR String in state.processed_catch_ids:
